## Interpretation and scope

## 1.1 In this Practice Direction –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (1) ‘the 1991 Act’ means the Road Traffic Act 1991;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (2) ‘the 1996 Act’ means the London Local Authorities Act 1996;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (3) ‘the Road User Charging Regulations’ means the Road User Charging (Enforcement and Adjudication) (London) Regulations 2001;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (4) ‘the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations’ means the Road Traffic (Vehicle Emissions) (Fixed Penalty) (England) Regulations 2002;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (5) ‘the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations’ means the Road Traffic (Vehicle Emissions) (Fixed Penalty) (Wales) Regulations 2003;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (6) ‘the 2003 Act’ means the London Local Authorities and Transport for London Act 2003;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (7) the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations’ means the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Approved Devices, Charging Guidelines and General Provisions) (England) Regulations 2022;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (8) the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations” means the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (General Provisions) (Wales) Regulations 2013;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (9) ‘the Representations and Appeals (England) Regulations’ means the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Representations and Appeals) (England) Regulations 2022;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (10) the Representations and Appeals (Wales) Regulations” means the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Representations and Appeals) (Wales) Regulations 2013;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (11) the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations’ means the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations 2012;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (12)  ‘the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations’ means the Road User Charging Schemes (Penalty Charges, Adjudication and Enforcement) (England) Regulations 2013 ; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.1 In this Practice Direction –] (13) ‘the Littering from Vehicles Regulations’ means the Littering From Vehicles Outside London (Keepers: Civil Penalties) Regulations 2018.

## 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (1) increased penalty charges provided for in parking charge certificates issued under paragraph 6 of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (2) amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication of a parking adjudicator pursuant to section 73 of the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (3) increased penalty charges provided for in a charge certificate issued under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1 to the 1996 Act (relating to a contravention or failure to comply with an order made under a provision referred to in section 4(2) of that Act reserving all or part of a carriageway of a road as a bus lane);

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (4) increased fixed penalties to which regulation 17(6) of the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations refer;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (5) amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication pursuant to the Schedule to the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (6) increased penalty charges provided for in charge certificates issued under regulation 17 of the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (7) increased fixed penalties to which regulation 17(6) of the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations refer;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (8) increased penalty charges provided for in charge certificates issued under regulation 21 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (9) increased penalty charges provided for in charge certificates issued under regulation 20 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (10) amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication pursuant to the Representations and Appeals (England) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (11) amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication pursuant to the Representations and Appeals (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (12) increased penalty charges provided for in charge certificates issued under regulation 3(1) of the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (13) amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication pursuant to the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (14) increased penalty charges provided for in charge certificates issued under regulation 17(1) of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.2 Part 75 applies to proceedings for the recovery of –] (15) the unpaid amount of a fixed penalty and any related costs awarded by an adjudicator pursuant to regulation 7(2) of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations.

## 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (1) ‘authority’ means the authority entitled to recover amounts due under the enactments referred to in paragraph 1.2;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (2) ‘notice of the amount due’ means, as the case may be –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (a) a parking charge certificate issued under paragraph 6 of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (b) a charge certificate issued under paragraph 8 of Schedule 1 to the 1996 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (c) a fixed penalty notice issued under regulations 10 or 13 of the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (d) a charge certificate issued under regulation 17 of the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (e) a fixed penalty notice issued under regulations 10 or 13 of the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (f) a charge certificate issued under regulation 21 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (g) a charge certificate issued under regulation 20 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (h) a charge certificate issued under regulation 3(1) of the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (i) a charge certificate issued under regulation 17(1) of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (j) an enforcement notice issued under regulation 6A(1) of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (3) ‘order’ means an order made under –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (a) paragraph 7 of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (b) paragraph 9 of Schedule 1 to the 1996 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (c) section 73(15) of the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (d) regulation 21 of the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (e) regulation 7 of the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (f) regulation 18 of the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (g) regulation 21 of the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (h) regulation 22 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (i) regulation 21 of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (j) regulation 16(1) of the Representations and Appeals (England) Regulations for any amount which is payable under an adjudicator’s adjudication; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (k) regulation 12(3)(a) of the Representations and Appeals (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (l) regulation 4 of the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (m) regulation 16 of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (n) regulation 18 of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (o) regulation 7(2)(b) of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (4) ‘respondent’ means –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (a) the person on whom the notice of the amount due was served; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 1.3 In Part 75 and this practice direction –] (b) the person (other than an authority) by whom the amount due under an adjudication is payable.

## Traffic Enforcement Centre

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Traffic Enforcement Centre] 2.1 All claims to which Part 75 applies must be filed at the Traffic Enforcement Centre (‘the Centre’) at 21/27 St. Katherine’s Street, Northampton. NN1 2LH.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Traffic Enforcement Centre] (Form TE7, Application to file a statement out of time/extension of time (Parking)) and form TE9, Witness statement – unpaid penalty charge (Parking), can be filed electronically at: tec@hmcts.gsi.gov.uk )

## Request

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Request] 3.1 Where an order in respect of amounts payable by a person other than an authority under an adjudication pursuant to –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Request] (a) section 73 of the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Request] (b) the Representations and Appeals (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Request] (c) the Representations and Appeals (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Request] (d) the Schedule to the Road User Charging Regulations; or (e) Part 4 of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations, is sought, rule 75.3 applies with the necessary modifications and, in addition, the request must— (i) state the date on which the adjudication was made; (ii) provide details of the order made on the adjudication; and (iii) certify the amount awarded by way of costs and that the amount remains unpaid.

## Service of Order

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Service of Order] 3A.1 Rule 75.3(5) requires the authority to serve the order within 15 days of the date on which the request is registered with the court. For clarity, the respondent must be served within 15 days and attention is drawn to the provisions of Part 6, particularly the provisions relating to deemed service.

## Functions of court officer

## 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (1) the district judge under –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (a) paragraphs 8(4) and (5)(d) of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (b) paragraphs 10(4) and (5)(d) of Schedule 1 to the 1996 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (c) regulations 19(4) and 19(5)(d) of the Road User Charging Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (d) regulations 23(4) and 23(5)(d) of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (f) regulations 22(4) and 22(5)(d) of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (h) regulations 5(4) and 5(5)(d) of the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (2) the court under –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (a) paragraph 23(3) of the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (b) paragraph 23(3) of the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (c) regulations 19(3) and 19(4)(d) of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 4.1 A court officer may exercise the functions of –] (d) regulations 7A(3) and 7A(4)(d) of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations.

## Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] 5.1 Paragraphs 5.2 to 5.5 apply where the respondent applies for an order allowing a longer period than 21 days to serve –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (1) a statutory declaration pursuant to –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (a) paragraph 8(3) of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (b) paragraph 10(3) of Schedule 1 to the 1996 Act;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (c) regulation 23(3) of the Vehicle Emissions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (d) regulation 19(3) of the Road User Charging Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (e) regulation 23(3) of the Vehicle Emissions (Wales) Regulations; or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (2) a witness statement pursuant to–

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (a) regulation 23(3) of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (England) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (b) regulation 22(3) of the Civil Enforcement of Road Traffic Contraventions (Wales) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (c) regulation 5(3) of the Penalty Charges Enforcement (London) Regulations;

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (d) regulation 19(3) of the Road User Charging Schemes (England) Regulations; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application for longer period for filing of statutory declaration or witness statement] (e) regulation 7A(3) of the Littering from Vehicles Regulations.

## 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] (1) a completed application notice (form PE2 (Application to File a Statutory Declaration Out of Time) may be used for applications relating to statutory declarations and form TE7 may be used for applications relating to witness statements); and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] (2) a completed –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] (a) statutory declaration in form PE3 (Statutory Declaration – unpaid penalty charge); or

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] (b) witness statement in form TE9.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] (Forms PE2, PE3, TE7 and TE9 can be obtained from Form Finder at https://hmctsformfinder.justice.gov.uk/HMCTS/FormFinder.do (opens in a new tab) and can also be obtained from the Traffic Enforcement Centre, 21/27 St. Katharine’s Street, Northampton NN1 2LH. (Telephone number: 0300 123 1059)

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] 5.3 The court will serve a copy of the application notice and a copy of the statutory declaration or witness statement on the authority that obtained the court order seeking representations on the application.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] 5.4 A court officer will deal with the application without a hearing. The matter will not be dealt with until at least 14 days after the date on which the application notice and statutory declaration or witness statement were served on the authority.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] 5.5 If the proceedings have been transferred to another court the Centre will transfer the application to that court.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 5.2 The respondent must send to the Centre –] 5.6 Paragraphs 5.3 to 5.5 do not apply where the court receives an application notice that is accompanied by a statutory declaration that is invalid by virtue of paragraph 8(2A) of Schedule 6 to the 1991 Act as inserted by section 15 of the 2003 Act.

## Application to review order made by court officer

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Application to review order made by court officer] 6.1 Where any order is made by a court officer it will contain a statement of the right of either party to request a review of the decision by a district judge.

## 6.2 Attention is drawn to rule 75.5A.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 6.2 Attention is drawn to rule 75.5A.] 6.3 Attention is drawn to the limited powers of a district judge where a request is made to review an order of a court officer refusing an application for further time for filing a statutory declaration or witness statement. Any review of that order by a district judge will only be a review of the decision to refuse the application for further time for filing a statutory declaration or witness statement. The review will not be a review of the validity of the notice of the amount due or any order within the meaning of paragraph 1.3(3) of this Practice Direction.

## Hearing

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Hearing] 7.1 When a hearing is to be held, the proceedings will be transferred to the County Court hearing centre which serves the respondent’s address for service. This transfer is only for the purposes of holding the hearing and serving any orders made as a result of the hearing.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Hearing] 7.2 The respondent’s address for service is the address for service shown on the application notice or, if more than one, the latest application notice.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > Hearing] 7.3 The County Court hearing centre where the hearing is held will serve any orders made as a result of the hearing before returning the papers to the Centre, or, if the proceedings have been transferred, to the County Court hearing centre where the proceedings have been transferred.

## 7.4 Evidence at any hearing may be given orally or by witness statement.

## Applications to suspend a local authority warrant of control

## 8.1 Where –

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 8.1 Where –] (1) the respondent makes an application under paragraph 5; and

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 8.1 Where –] (2) before that application is determined, a local authority warrant of control is issued,

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 8.1 Where –] the local authority must suspend enforcement of the local authority warrant of control until the application for an extension order is determined.

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 8.1 Where –] (Rule 75.8(b) provides that, where an order is deemed to have been revoked following the filing of a statutory declaration or witness statement, any execution issued on the order will cease to have effect.)

[PRACTICE DIRECTION 75 – TRAFFIC ENFORCEMENT > 8.1 Where –] Updated: Tuesday, 31 May 2022
